From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pkgdemon <jpm820@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 04:10:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] NextBSD: loader, the Startup Manager

The graphical Startup Manager (nextbsd/nextbsd-freebsd-compat#95): every
installed version of NextBSD (each a ZFS boot environment) as a disk on
the boot screen, in the boot screen's own colour (bootsplash_style: black
for NextBSD's splash, grey for Gershwin's).

- Every graphical start with more than one version shows it for
  nextbsd_startup_delay seconds (3; 0 or NO for the logo alone), counting
  down as the loader's prompt does; any key stops the count, and at zero
  the usual version starts.
- Option (Alt) held while starting opens it with no count. Option is a
  modifier on its own, so loader.efi reads keys through the extended input
  protocol with EFI_KEY_STATE_EXPOSED, which asks the firmware for partial
  keystrokes; it tells Lua with nextbsd_startup_manager=option.
- boot -r at the prompt opens it where there is a framebuffer (the
  numbered list otherwise).
- Left and right choose, Return starts the chosen version once (as
  bootenv does: nothing on disk changes), V and S add a verbose or
  single-user start, Esc opens the prompt.

The pieces:

- gfx_fb_text(), gfx.fb_text() and gfx.fb_font(): text in the console
  font in an exact colour with nothing behind the glyphs (console text
  always fills its cells with a palette colour), and the font cell and
  framebuffer size for laying it out.
- boot-video keyboard: GRAPHICS_MODE ignores the keyboard (0019); the
  Startup Manager takes it while it shows.
- stand/lua/startup.lua, called from loader.lua and cli.lua under pcall,
  so an error in it is printed and the boot goes on.
- nextbsd-startup-{disk,sel,go}[-dark][@2x].png in stand/images (carried
  in src-overlay/).

Carried out-of-tree for NextBSD.
---
diff --git a/stand/common/gfx_fb.c b/stand/common/gfx_fb.c
index 71a636109..8e81a41e6 100644
--- a/stand/common/gfx_fb.c
+++ b/stand/common/gfx_fb.c
@@ -1593,6 +1593,67 @@ gfx_fb_fill_rgb(uint32_t x1, uint32_t y1, uint32_t x2, uint32_t y2,
 	    y2 - y1, 0));
 }
 
+/*
+ * NextBSD: a line of text in the console font at (x, y), in an exact
+ * 24-bit colour, with nothing behind the glyphs, so it sits on whatever
+ * is already there (the Startup Manager's names on its grey).  Console
+ * text always fills its cells with a palette colour; this does not.
+ * Returns the width drawn in pixels, 0 when nothing was drawn.
+ */
+uint32_t
+gfx_fb_text(const char *s, uint32_t x, uint32_t y, uint32_t rgb)
+{
+#if defined(EFI)
+	EFI_GRAPHICS_OUTPUT_BLT_PIXEL *buf, *p;
+#else
+	struct paletteentry *buf, *p;
+#endif
+	teken_attr_t a;
+	const uint8_t *glyph;
+	uint32_t fw, fh, bpl, len, width, i, gx, gy;
+
+	if (gfx_state.tg_fb_type == FB_TEXT || s == NULL)
+		return (0);
+	fw = gfx_state.tg_font.vf_width;
+	fh = gfx_state.tg_font.vf_height;
+	len = strlen(s);
+	if (fw == 0 || fh == 0 || len == 0 ||
+	    x >= gfx_state.tg_fb.fb_width ||
+	    y + fh > gfx_state.tg_fb.fb_height)
+		return (0);
+	if (x + len * fw > gfx_state.tg_fb.fb_width)
+		len = (gfx_state.tg_fb.fb_width - x) / fw;
+	if (len == 0)
+		return (0);
+	width = len * fw;
+	buf = calloc(width * fh, sizeof(*buf));
+	if (buf == NULL)
+		return (0);
+	memset(&a, 0, sizeof(a));
+	bpl = (fw + 7) / 8;
+	for (i = 0; i < len; i++) {
+		glyph = font_lookup(&gfx_state.tg_font,
+		    (teken_char_t)(unsigned char)s[i], &a);
+		if (glyph == NULL)
+			continue;
+		for (gy = 0; gy < fh; gy++) {
+			for (gx = 0; gx < fw; gx++) {
+				if ((glyph[gy * bpl + gx / 8] &
+				    (0x80 >> (gx % 8))) == 0)
+					continue;
+				p = &buf[gy * width + i * fw + gx];
+				p->Red = (rgb >> 16) & 0xff;
+				p->Green = (rgb >> 8) & 0xff;
+				p->Blue = rgb & 0xff;
+				p->Reserved = 0xff;
+			}
+		}
+	}
+	gfx_fb_cons_display(x, y, width, fh, buf);
+	free(buf);
+	return (width);
+}
+
 /*
  * draw rectangle in framebuffer using gfx coordinates.
  */
